response:
 Here we are looking for the number of ways to choose 4 members out of 25, which is a combination problem. A combination of n items taken r at a time i.e. {eq}{^n}C_r

{/eq} is defined as the number of ways to choose r items out of n items without regard to order. {eq}{^n}C_r = \dfrac{n!}{(n-r)!\ r!}

{/eq}

As we can see from the problem given above, we need to find the number of ways to choose 4 members out of 25 without regard to order. That is,

{eq}\begin{align}

{^{25}}C_4 &= \dfrac{25!}{(25-4)! \times 4!} \\

&= \dfrac{25!}{21! \times 4!} \\

&= \dfrac{25 \times 24 \times 23 \times 22 \times 21!}{21! \times 4!} \\

&=  25 \times 4 \times 22 \times 23 \\

&= 30,300\\

\end{align}

{/eq}

The number of ways to choose members to form a 4-person executive committee is: {eq}30,300

{/eq}

